     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"Every route to exfiltration is blocked by mfa_admin. Exfiltration needs admin_db (via exfiltrate_db) or admin_fileserver (via exfiltrate_fileserver). Each of these needs a foothold on the db or fileserver, gained through auth_db or auth_fileserver, and both of those require stolen_dbadmin. The only source of stolen_dbadmin is dump_dbadmin_dc, which requires admin_dc. admin_dc comes only from escalate_dc, which requires foothold_dc. The only source of foothold_dc is auth_dc, which requires NOT mfa_admin. Since mfa:admin is deployed, auth_dc can never fire, so foothold_dc, admin_dc, stolen_dbadmin and the db/fileserver footholds stay false, and exfiltrated is unreachable. The attacker can still get footholds on the web server, proxy and workstation, reach the internal network, compromise the appserver and kerberoast stolen_admin, but this does not lead to exfiltration.\"}"
    }
